From 27481b30bae844fe9d683fec6bee7e1d102a14eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maxime <maxime.lefrancois@emse.fr>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:02:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Add a base_iri option for the relative IRIs of a mapping

A mapping without @base or rml:baseIRI had its relative IRIs resolved
against http://example.com/base/, written in the code. The base IRI is an
input of an RML processor: the RML-Core test cases RMLTC0019a, RMLTC0022c
and RMLTC0026b (kg-construct/rml-core) give it as http://example.com/ in
their metadata, so they cannot pass with the fixed base.

The option base_iri of the [datasets] section of the configuration file
now sets it; without it, the base is http://example.com/base/ as before.
